    "title": "2026-06-10-post-mortem-visuals · candidate-010 (muted palette + 20px grid)"
  },
  "agent": {
    "note": "Iter 10 — three changes per your feedback. (a) Muted both palette tones: orange #ef7525 → #d96b22 (rustier), gray #4b5563 → #3a414a (closer to bg). Avatar variants shifted proportionally. (b) All rect positions and sizes snapped to a 20px grid — Draw Mode will snap your additions to the same grid, so any rects you draw to respond to me will align cleanly with mine. (c) Layout convention shift: both agent and human bodies now anchor at x=80 (same grid column); avatars distinguish sides (agent at x=20 left, human at x=700 right). The asymmetric 28px right margin is the cost of 768 not being 20-divisible — accepted vs. forcing off-grid positions. Also shipped: editor canvas-bg fallback fix so the file's derive.background actually paints behind the rects (not just shown in the panel). Verify by checking that the canvas behind the rects is now your #14151b not the theme purple.",
    "question": "Color intensities about right, or want them muted further? Layout grid alignment readable when you turn on Draw mode (snap should match)? Bg fix landing properly (canvas dark #14151b vs editor default purple)? If all three feel right, next we're ready to wire this layout into the actual post-mortem template chat-stream.",
    "context": {
      "category": {
        "kind": "known",
        "value": "color-palette-exploration"
      },
      "intent": {
        "action": "refine",
        "summary": "mute palette + 20px grid alignment + canvas-bg fix"
      },
      "relation": {
        "kind": "refines",
        "target": "009"
      },
      "layoutIntent": "free"
    },
    "response": {
      "body": "Approved. when we assemble the template, we likely can get further DSL char savings by packing non-overlapping rectangles into less layers.",
      "from": "human",
      "at": "2026-06-10T04:27:02.049Z"
    }
  },
